#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# stirling_s1

#% text
# `stirling_s1(n, k)` gives the signed Stirling number of the first kind.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `(-1)^(n - k)*stirling_s1(n, k)` counts the permutations of `n` elements with exactly `k` cycles (DLMF 26.8). `stirling_s1(n, k)` is the coefficient of `x^k` in the falling factorial `x*(x - 1)*...*(x - n + 1)`.

#% item
# `stirling_s1` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
stirling_s1(5, 2)
#% output
#= -50

#% cell
stirling_s1(5, 5)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
stirling_s1(4, range(4))
#% output
#= [-6, 11, -6, 1]

#% cell
stirling_s1(30, 10)
#% output
#= 215760462268683520394805979744

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The coefficients of the falling factorial:

#% cell
coefficient_list(expand(product(x - j, [j, 0, 4])), x)
#% output
#= [0, 24, -50, 35, -10, 1]

#% cell
stirling_s1(5, range(0, 5))
#% output
#= [0, 24, -50, 35, -10, 1]

#% text
# The absolute values add up to `n!`:

#% cell
[sum(abs(stirling_s1(6, range(6)))), factorial(6)]
#% output
#= [720, 720]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `stirling_s2`, `factorial`, `binomial`
